<title>USA: World Bank approves loan for Mexico pension reform.</title>
<headline>World Bank approves loan for Mexico pension reform.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank said Wednesday it had approved a $400 million loan to support Mexico's pension system reform.</p>
<p>The program, which will be co-financed by a $300 million loan from the Inter-American Development Bank, will set up a privately managed and fully funded pension system for some 10 million Mexican private sector workers.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that the Mexican plan was modeled after Chile's 1981 pension reform, which covered both private and public sector workers.</p>
<p>&quot;The reform of the social security system is one of the most important reforms undertaken by the Mexican government,&quot; the bank said in a press release.</p>
<p>&quot;It will ensure long-term financial viability of the old age insurance system, foster a more equitable pension system and serve to attract Mexico's workforce into the formal economy under better labor conditions,&quot; it added.</p>
</text>
